# dotfiles-core/.gitignore — Core is config only; never machine state or secrets.
*.log
*.bak
.DS_Store
# machine-specific overrides never sync up to Core
zsh/99-local.zsh
# generated by `make setup` from scripts/tool-versions.env (repo-local dev toolchain)
mise.local.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Claude Code: ignore local/transient session state, but DO track the shared
# Claude-Code-on-the-web setup (the SessionStart hook that provisions the gate
# toolchain + its settings) and the shared maintenance routines (slash commands +
# subagents) so every session — local or remote — has them. settings.local.json
# stays ignored (it's per-machine).
#
# EVERY SHARED FILE NEEDS ITS OWN NEGATION, and a top-level file needs one even when
# the routine that reads it is already negated. `.claude/*` matches files as well as
# directories, so tool-decisions.md — the decided-and-rejected ledger #661 taught
# /tool-scout to read — was written, referenced from three places, and never tracked
# (#700). The directory negations below made that invisible: commands/ and agents/
# were negated, so the files POINTING at the ledger vendored out fine while the ledger
# itself did not. Adding a shared file here means adding its line here too;
# audit-core.sh §1b is the backstop that says so out loud.
.claude/*
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/tool-decisions.md
.claude/settings.local.json
